1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,655
Today there's a small blue teardrop

2
00:00:02,675 --> 00:00:04,683
over some people's heads.

3
00:00:04,703 --> 00:00:06,633
It takes you until lunch to work out

4
00:00:06,653 --> 00:00:08,053
what it means.

5
00:00:08,363 --> 00:00:09,443
They've cried.

6
00:00:09,463 --> 00:00:10,752
Because of you.

7
00:00:10,772 --> 00:00:12,687
The bus driver has one.

8
00:00:12,707 --> 00:00:14,572
Your mum has forty-one.

9
00:00:15,163 --> 00:00:16,743
Your best friend got hers…

10
00:00:16,763 --> 00:00:17,751
last night.

11
00:00:20,801 --> 00:00:22,306
At first you think it's a trick of the

12
00:00:22,326 --> 00:00:23,265
light.

13
00:00:23,285 --> 00:00:25,415
The man at the bakery, nothing.

14
00:00:25,435 --> 00:00:27,475
The woman with the dog, nothing.

15
00:00:27,495 --> 00:00:28,815
The bus driver.

16
00:00:28,835 --> 00:00:30,065
One teardrop.

17
00:00:30,085 --> 00:00:30,892
And a look.

18
00:00:30,912 --> 00:00:31,645
You.

19
00:00:31,665 --> 00:00:32,305
Me?

20
00:00:32,325 --> 00:00:32,955
Route nine.

21
00:00:32,975 --> 00:00:33,925
Six years ago.

22
00:00:33,965 --> 00:00:35,130
You paid in pennies.

23
00:00:35,150 --> 00:00:36,525
A hundred and forty of them.

24
00:00:36,545 --> 00:00:37,355
In the rain.

25
00:00:37,375 --> 00:00:38,641
That made you cry?

26
00:00:38,661 --> 00:00:40,360
It was my first day.

27
00:00:40,510 --> 00:00:41,940
So that's the rule.

28
00:00:41,960 --> 00:00:44,415
A teardrop for everyone who's ever cried

29
00:00:44,435 --> 00:00:45,810
because of you.

30
00:00:45,835 --> 00:00:47,530
And a number, if it happened more than

31
00:00:47,550 --> 00:00:48,466
once.

32
00:00:48,486 --> 00:00:49,740
Your old landlord.

33
00:00:49,760 --> 00:00:50,516
Three.

34
00:00:50,536 --> 00:00:51,587
You know why.

35
00:00:53,077 --> 00:00:54,857
A stranger in the park.

36
00:00:54,877 --> 00:00:55,617
One.

37
00:00:55,637 --> 00:00:57,217
You have never seen her before in your

38
00:00:57,237 --> 00:00:57,958
life.

39
00:00:58,708 --> 00:01:00,188
You decide to fix it.

40
00:01:00,208 --> 00:01:02,231
One apology per teardrop.

41
00:01:02,251 --> 00:01:03,962
I'm sorry about the pennies.

42
00:01:03,982 --> 00:01:05,618
Took you six years.

43
00:01:05,768 --> 00:01:07,588
The teardrop stays.

44
00:01:07,608 --> 00:01:09,563
Apologies don't delete them.

45
00:01:09,583 --> 00:01:11,138
They just sit next to them.

46
00:01:12,128 --> 00:01:13,193
Then, your mum.

47
00:01:13,213 --> 00:01:14,243
Forty-one.

48
00:01:14,263 --> 00:01:14,843
Mum.

49
00:01:14,863 --> 00:01:16,209
I need to say sorry.

50
00:01:16,229 --> 00:01:17,424
What did you break?

51
00:01:17,444 --> 00:01:18,074
Nothing!

52
00:01:18,094 --> 00:01:19,124
For all of it.

53
00:01:19,144 --> 00:01:21,164
I made you cry forty-one times.

54
00:01:21,184 --> 00:01:21,934
Forty-one?

55
00:01:21,974 --> 00:01:22,807
Is that all?

56
00:01:22,827 --> 00:01:23,757
Sweetheart.

57
00:01:23,777 --> 00:01:25,257
Half of those were your school plays.

58
00:01:25,277 --> 00:01:26,655
You were a very moving tree.

59
00:01:26,675 --> 00:01:27,532
A tree.

60
00:01:27,552 --> 00:01:29,256
And the day you left for the city.

61
00:01:29,276 --> 00:01:30,901
That one was sad crying.

62
00:01:30,921 --> 00:01:32,576
That one was proud crying.

63
00:01:32,596 --> 00:01:33,851
You'd know the difference if you called

64
00:01:33,871 --> 00:01:34,418
more.

65
00:01:34,438 --> 00:01:35,543
Like last week.

66
00:01:35,563 --> 00:01:37,121
When you called for no reason.

67
00:01:37,871 --> 00:01:39,301
You look at the number again.

68
00:01:39,321 --> 00:01:41,061
It doesn't say which kind.

69
00:01:41,081 --> 00:01:42,172
It never did.

70
00:01:43,662 --> 00:01:45,667
The stranger in the park.

71
00:01:45,687 --> 00:01:48,167
Two winters ago, you handed in a lost

72
00:01:48,187 --> 00:01:50,587
wallet, and never thought about it again.

73
00:01:51,637 --> 00:01:53,467
Which leaves one teardrop.

74
00:01:53,487 --> 00:01:54,352
Mira's.

75
00:01:54,372 --> 00:01:55,637
Last night's.

76
00:01:55,657 --> 00:01:57,287
She's back for the weekend.

77
00:01:57,307 --> 00:01:59,196
You thought dinner went fine.

78
00:01:59,216 --> 00:02:01,471
You said her new place sounded small.

79
00:02:01,491 --> 00:02:03,721
You said the course sounded hard.

80
00:02:03,741 --> 00:02:06,481
You joked that she'd forget you by Christmas.

81
00:02:06,501 --> 00:02:08,222
It has to be one of those.

82
00:02:08,311 --> 00:02:09,766
You buy flowers.

83
00:02:09,786 --> 00:02:12,067
Then you decide flowers look guilty.

84
00:02:12,087 --> 00:02:13,570
You leave them on a bench.

85
00:02:14,479 --> 00:02:15,884
You're doing the face again.

86
00:02:15,904 --> 00:02:16,359
Okay.

87
00:02:16,379 --> 00:02:18,084
Did I say something last night?

88
00:02:18,104 --> 00:02:19,065
Something wrong?

89
00:02:19,085 --> 00:02:19,365
What?

90
00:02:19,385 --> 00:02:19,963
No.

91
00:02:19,983 --> 00:02:20,858
You're sure?

92
00:02:20,878 --> 00:02:21,974
Because if I did

93
00:02:21,994 --> 00:02:23,327
Why would you think that?

94
00:02:23,977 --> 00:02:26,172
You can't say, because there's a teardrop

95
00:02:26,192 --> 00:02:27,397
over your head.

96
00:02:27,417 --> 00:02:29,361
So you say the other true thing.

97
00:02:29,381 --> 00:02:30,886
Because I'd want to know.

98
00:02:30,906 --> 00:02:32,648
If I ever made you cry.

99
00:02:33,348 --> 00:02:34,943
Okay, that's unfair.

100
00:02:34,963 --> 00:02:35,814
How did you know?

101
00:02:35,834 --> 00:02:36,739
I found the card.

102
00:02:36,759 --> 00:02:38,429
In the box you packed.

103
00:02:38,449 --> 00:02:40,489
For when it's Monday and you hate it.

104
00:02:40,509 --> 00:02:42,419
I read it on my new kitchen floor, and

105
00:02:42,439 --> 00:02:43,556
cried like an idiot.

106
00:02:43,576 --> 00:02:45,158
I forgot I wrote that.

107
00:02:45,178 --> 00:02:46,014
I didn't.

108
00:02:46,034 --> 00:02:47,532
What did it even say?

109
00:02:47,552 --> 00:02:49,052
It said, you're allowed to hate it,

110
00:02:49,072 --> 00:02:50,207
and stay anyway.

111
00:02:50,707 --> 00:02:51,909
That's pretty good.

112
00:02:51,929 --> 00:02:52,713
Don't.

113
00:02:53,663 --> 00:02:55,168
The teardrop's still there.

114
00:02:55,188 --> 00:02:56,475
You hope it stays.

115
00:02:57,165 --> 00:02:59,745
In the café window, your own reflection.

116
00:02:59,765 --> 00:03:02,161
And over your head, small and blue,

117
00:03:02,751 --> 00:03:04,748
you know exactly whose that is.

118
00:03:07,138 --> 00:03:08,627
Would you want to know?
